; Non-empty containers buried in nested detection positions that a per-variant hand-walk of the
; rust_structs missed but `visit_all_rust_types` reaches. Pins that the `non_empty` /
; `non_empty_map` runtime module + import wiring is pulled in for these shapes (a missing import
; would leave the generated crate referencing `NonEmptyVec` / `NonEmptyMap` undeclared).
;
; nested_plus  — a named array rule with a `*` (non-`+`) outer occurrence whose ELEMENT is an inline
;                `[+ uint]`. The old vec walker's `RustStructType::Array` arm checked only the
;                struct's own `bounds` (None here) and never the `element_type`, so the `[+]` was
;                invisible to that arm; the transparent alias `Vec<NonEmptyVec<u64>>` masked it. The
;                visitor walks the element type and sees it directly.
; dom_nonempty_map — a table whose `*` occurrence keeps it a loose map but whose DOMAIN (key) is an
;                inline `{+ uint => uint}`. The old map walker's `Table` arm checked `bounds` + the
;                `range` but never the `domain`, so a non-empty map on the key side was invisible to
;                that arm; the visitor walks the domain.
; holder       — embeds both so they also emit in member (record-field) position.
nested_plus = [* [+ uint]]
dom_nonempty_map = { * {+ uint => uint} => text }
holder = [np: nested_plus, dm: dom_nonempty_map]
